# Is the declared incompatibility with Work Tab still real?
#
# About.xml names Fluffy.WorkTab in <incompatibleWith>, and this set exists to go and look rather
# than to trust a declaration that nobody has replayed.
#
# Read green-is-good, like every other set. The scenarios for this one assert the DOCUMENTED
# SYMPTOM - the window that opens is not this mod's, or the error the conflict produces is
# logged - carrying @allow-errors so the expected error does not fail them by itself. Green means
# the incompatibility is still what About.xml claims; red means something moved. Letting the
# ordinary suite go red instead was the first design here, and it fails for one reason: an
# expected red and an accidental red are the same colour.
#
# Those scenarios are NOT written yet. The first run of this set plays the ordinary suite, which
# is exploration - it says which scenarios break and how, and that is what the assertions get
# written from.
#
# Replayed when WORK TAB moves, not when Work Studio is published: it is their update that stales
# the verdict, not ours.
#
# packageId is what that mod's own About.xml carries, read on 2026-09-21 from the installed copy -
# not inferred from its Workshop title, which reads "Fluffy's Work Tab (yet another fork)" while
# the mod itself is named "Work Tab" and keeps the original packageId. That is exactly why this
# had to be read rather than guessed.
#
# The staging activates these before Work Studio, which is the order that matters: the button patch
# resolves the Work tab's window class at startup, so the replacement has to be in place first.
#
# packageId      workshopId   what it is
Fluffy.WorkTab   3552152340   Work Tab, the declared incompatibility
